Z||000000||DXR_DAD||03-02-2000||11:57 PM||||In another post Trubo86SE talked about a list of fiero mechanics, to ad to this, Repair shops,parts,info, etc. Can we come up with a list, with contact names of people that we have done business with and have faith in their abilities. In the last few days I have read a few post that were not to comforting when it comes to "Fiero Shops/Parts/Services". Owning two fieros this didn't sound to good. If we all have some good shops with good people, then please tell. Let us know who to go to and who not to deal with. some of us are close enough to each other but still don't know who's who in the world of fieros. This may help<P>This is just my thoughts????||||reg||5
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||03-03-2000||12:05 AM||||I'd gladly host a list like this on my site, perhaps we could have mirrors of it on various other sites as well?||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||03-03-2000||12:34 AM||||I was even thinking,  what about that little tire shop down the street that fixed a flat for you for free! and doesn't charge extra just because its a fiero! I think everyone has a story like this and these are the people that we don't know about.<P>Does any one have a Joe's Junk Yard.......you know, the only people that work there is Joe and his dog.  Joe is 75yrs old and his dog is about the same. He gives away more car parts than he sales  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000003||Phaeton||03-03-2000||02:51 AM||||I noticed a member in North Pole, right down the road a little.<BR>At Tip Top Chevrolet (farthest north chevy dealer in the world) works Topper, their drivability and diagnostic man.  He is good, he will figure the Fiero, and the explanation will make sense.  Insist on him by name and be ready to pay dealer shop rate.||||reg||6
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||03-03-2000||10:32 AM||||Here's one, The guy that polished my wheels:<BR>Cantwell's Fabricators. His name is Dave Cantwell, location: South San Francisco, CA<BR>He is a good Metal worker and knows his stuff. Likes to do odd jobs that no one wants to touch! He's Working on face plates for me as we speak  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> .||||reg||14
Z||000005||Gokart||03-04-2000||07:05 AM||||Unfortunatly I have only places NOT to go to. I've had my car serviced at 4 different places and have been totally unsatified in one way or another. The only "Fiero Angel" I've come across so far was Cobra! Most of you do not live in Mass. so you won't have to worry about the places I've had problems with, but if you add this to your site DaRkLoRD I'd be happy to give the business titles.||||reg||8
Z||000006||1FST2M6||03-04-2000||12:23 PM||||my $.02  The only shop that touches my car along with 5 other fieros. I'd put them up there.. And the owner even said the wouldn't mind being known as "Fiero Tolerant" he said "Fiero Friendly" was too strong a word cause parts are difficult to get.. but he also says the same about my Alfa 164... <P>Engineered Performance Inc. <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> <BR>Smyrna, Ga <BR>770-434-0051 <BR>ask for Glenn or Ed  tell them your a friend of Travis' <BR>They have 7 ASE techs on staff now. And 4 are ASE Master techs. Have 3 degrees from Georgia Tech 2 in ME (Mechanical Engineering)and one in Physics. Held by the owners. I'd recommend them to anyone for anything... from oil changes to Custom Twin Turbo setups... ||||reg||1
Z||000007||DXR_DAD||03-04-2000||12:37 PM||||DaRkLoRD, can we just post all the info here? or would you like us to e-mail you? I have 2 or 3 more places here in So.SF.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Carolina 88GT||03-04-2000||01:07 PM||||Would like to give out my mech's name, but lemme check with them first.  Some people like to be told that their name is going on some form of list.||||reg||14
Z||000009||stimpy||03-04-2000||01:30 PM||||I would like to give props to Automotive Service Center in Mustang OK, they did the machine work on my motor, along with MustangFirestone who did the assembly and install. Very reputable professional guys who where not in the least intimidated by Fieros.<BR> Also, he must be being modest right now, but forum member Big O (aka my dad) will repair any tire if repairable for free, no matter where it was bought. So if you are travelng down I5 through the central Valley of CA, check out the BigO tire store on Prescott Rd in Modesto.<BR>(the preceeding has been a totally shameless plug. But he does have a really cool supercharged 86 GT.)||||reg||1
Z||000010||DXR_DAD||03-04-2000||01:44 PM||||I hope his tire repairs aren't shameless plugs. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I had to do it!!||||reg||10
Z||000012||DaRkLoRD||03-04-2000||04:14 PM||||Posting here is probably the best way, I just need the contact info in a fairly standard format. also include any specific contact names if you'd like.<P>eg.<BR>joe's auto shop<BR>123 fiero road, unit 3<BR>city, state/province<BR>phone number<BR>email/web site - if applicable<P>Adding a section for places to avoid would also be a good idea, but it should probably be mentioned whether they should just be avoided for Fiero repairs or just in general.<P>Thanks.. the Fiero Project wouldn't even exist without you people providing valuable info like this.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>btw, I've emailed my web host about upgrading the server, I'll hopefully hear back from them by monday night..||||reg||1
Z||000013||DXR_DAD||03-04-2000||09:01 PM||||TAYLORMADE AUTOMOTIVE<BR>Chris Gibbs<BR>1361B San Mateo Ave <BR>So. San Francisco, ca 94080<BR>(650) 871-2022<BR>All his mechanics are ASE Certified, They support Skyline College Auto Tech Program.<BR>The only shop That I know of that does it all! and I mean ALL, Chris has had 3 car in the Oakland Roadster Shows, one in the just passed show. They have build many hot rods and roadsters here in the So.SF area. And the part I like about this place is the floors are so clean you can eat off them <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> and lots of rods to look at, T's, Buckets, A's, 55,56,57 Chevys,Vetts,etc. even the old Sees Candy Cars & Cycle are repaired there. Chris is one cool guy he always has time to talk about cars!!!||||reg||1
